@page "/help"

<PageTitle>Help & Documentation - Vi-RMM</PageTitle>

<div class="page-container">
    <div class="page-header">
        <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Documentation</div>
            <h1>Vi-RMM Help Center & User Manual</h1>
            <p>Complete guide for managing endpoints, deploying agents, and utilizing remote management features.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-card">
            <h3>⚡ Real-Time Features Overview</h3>
            <ul style="padding-left:20px;line-height:1.8;font-size:13px;">
                <li><strong>Live Command Terminal</strong>: Interactive PowerShell & CMD execution with live output streaming.</li>
                <li><strong>Remote Desktop</strong>: Live desktop frame capture with mouse and keyboard input control.</li>
                <li><strong>Remote File Manager</strong>: Browse, download, upload, create folders, and delete remote files.</li>
                <li><strong>Process & Service Control</strong>: Terminate rogue processes and start/stop/restart Windows services.</li>
                <li><strong>Automated Health Checks</strong>: Continuous evaluation of Defender, Firewall, Disks, CPU, and Event Logs.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-card">
            <h3>🚀 Agent Deployment Guide</h3>
            <p>Deploy the agent via the <a href="/agents/install" style="color:#22c7d6;">Install Agent</a> page.</p>
            <div class="code-copy-box" style="margin: 10px 0;">
                <code>Vi-RMM.Agent.exe --install --server &lt;server-url&gt;</code>
            </div>
            <p class="muted">Runs as a background Windows Service named <code>ViRMMAgent</code>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-card">
            <h3>ℹ️ About Vi-RMM</h3>
            <p><strong>Vi-RMM Web Console & Endpoint Management Agent</strong></p>
            <p>Version: 1.0.0 Final</p>
            <p>Platform: .NET 10 / ASP.NET Core Blazor / SignalR</p>
            <p class="muted">All features clickable, live, and real-time capable.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
